    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling core, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29), who is our clear standout play. Facing Aaron Civale, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive park factor boost and favorable winds, combined with a strong platoon advantage that elevates his base projection significantly. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (76.41) provides an elite anchor against the vulnerable Kochanowicz, bolstered by an excellent 5.14 xERA matchup and strong xwOBA metrics. **Kyle Tucker** (75.75) remains a must-start despite the presence of Spencer Strider on the mound; the raw talent and positive SP skill adjustment outweigh the matchup difficulty, confirming his status as an every-day staple for the Waves.\n\nOptimization decisions today heavily favored lineup spots and park-adjusted efficiency. **Jackson Merrill** (73.87) secured his place in the outfield due to his high-leverage leadoff spot and a solid platoon edge against Dustin May, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (68.57) and **Andy Pages** (68.65) round out the high-efficiency tier. The tightest call on the bench was **Brady House** (54.99), who pushed hard for a start against Janson Junk. Ultimately, **Brady House** was relegated to the pine because his adjusted efficiency lagged slightly behind the higher-upside profiles of **Jacob Wilson** and **Coby Mayo**, both of whom benefit from the specific park factors in play today.\n\nWe are navigating several risks heading into first pitch, most notably the prevalence of \"Lineup Pending\" status across the board. While we have projected positions for **Drake Baldwin**, **Liam Hicks**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Coby Mayo**, **Kyle Tucker**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Andy Pages**, and **Sam Antonacci**, any deviation in their official batting order could compress their efficiency scores. Furthermore, while **Jackson Merrill** is a high-upside play, managers should monitor his stolen base opportunities; his score accounts for an \"Elite Hold SP\" warning, reflecting the risk of facing a pitcher who effectively limits the run game. We remain comfortable with this configuration, provided weather patterns remain stable and the expected lineups hold.",
